# Usually not needed: on first visit mergit walks you through creating its
# GitHub App (with `npm run dev`, register a localhost app; with
# `npm run dev:fake-github`, everything is local and fake).
#
# Copy to .dev.vars only to supply an existing app's credentials by hand.
# These take priority over the in-app setup. Never commit .dev.vars.
# GITHUB_APP_ID=123456
# GITHUB_APP_SLUG=your-mergit-app
# GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=Iv23li...
# GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET=...
# The private key as base64 on one line:  base64 < app.private-key.pem | tr -d '\n'
# GITHUB_APP_PRIVATE_KEY=LS0tLS1CRUdJTi...

# Optional: require this code before anyone can run the first-time setup.
# SETUP_TOKEN=some-long-random-string
